+# Making Solo Work Sustainable
+
+## Core idea
+
+Turn an empty, stressful workbench into a calm solo-business control system. Each narration beat adds one practical piece—pipeline, intake, templates, review, and boundaries—until the full system is visible and the founder has room to work.
+
+## Visual arc
+
+1. **Reactive:** loose tasks and messages orbit an unprotected founder.
+2. **Simple system:** a five-part operating rail assembles one useful layer at a time.
+3. **Sustainable:** time and scope guardrails close around the system, leaving a clear weekly plan.
+
+## Direction
+
+Use crisp editorial diagrams, large type, and restrained card choreography on paper and navy fields. Motion should feel like organizing a desk: items sort, align, and lock into place. No stock footage, decorative dashboards, or generic AI imagery.
+
+## Narration beats
+
+Fifteen timed beats carry the refined lesson narration. Each beat has one primary visual action and remains readable without narration.
