+# Design: Making Solo Work Sustainable
+
+## Frame system
+
+- 1920×1080 canvas with a 120px frame inset and a reserved 120px footer.
+- Alternate paper and deep-navy fields to separate problem, build, and resolve phases.
+- A persistent five-node rail provides continuity through the middle of the lesson.
+
+## Typography
+
+- Proxima Nova with the supplied system fallback.
+- Display: 104px / 900; headings: 68px / 900; body: 42px / 400; labels: 22px / 700 uppercase.
+- Keep line lengths short and use gold only for decisions, active nodes, and guardrails.
+
+## Palette
+
+- Navy `#0d2437` and deep navy `#0a1e2f` for foundations.
+- Blue `#3393d6` for systems and links.
+- Gold `#eaab2d` for active choices and boundaries.
+- Paper `#ffffff`, cultured `#f6f6f9`, and ink `#292f35` for readable working surfaces.
+
+## Motion
+
+- Each beat enters in 0.45–0.60 seconds and settles within 1.2 seconds.
+- Cards translate and fade; rules draw from left; nodes pop once. No infinite motion.
+- The final second adds a gold boundary lock and a small “SUSTAINABLE” seal.
+
+## Accessibility
+
+- Body copy never drops below 40px; labels remain at least 20px.
+- High-contrast text and redundant number, word, and shape cues communicate state.
+- Narration is stored verbatim in timed clip nodes.
